  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 106 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nMid-level ridging continues propagating eastward and should be \ncentered over the Southern Plains by Sunday. A disturbance in the \nnorthern Gulf looks to make its way westward towards the Texas coast \nand eventually undercuts the ridge which then allows it to \nflatten/elongate towards the Middle Mississippi Valley early next \nweek. It's still quite a bit unclear if this disturbance will impact \nour area bringing with it some rain/storm chances as models don't \nhave a good handle on this just yet. What is more certain is our \ntypical seabreeze pattern looks to make a return by Tuesday mainly \naffecting areas over the Coastal Plains. For everyone else expect a \nmainly dry and continued hot weather pattern to close out August and \nbegin the month of September.",
